<title>USA: USDA seeks comment on cotton imports.</title>
<headline>USDA seeks comment on cotton imports.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Agriculture Department Thursday said it was seeking public comment on whether U.S. regulations on cotton and cotton product imports need to be changed since they have not been amended since 1962.</p>
<p>The rules are aimed at preventing imported cotton and cotton covers from introducing foreign agricultural pests.</p>
<p>&quot;It's our goal to update and streamline the process without jeopardizing U.S. agriculture,&quot; said Alfred Elder, an official at USDA's Animal Plant and Health Inspection Service.</p>
<p>USDA seeks feedback on whether to allow commercial import of seed cotton, among other questions.</p>
